WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000 position:98%
What is important in our work is the fact that we can do everything with Mathematica.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Originally, I am an engineer,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.000 position:97%
and I started in continuum mechanics, including the mechanics of structural materials.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000 position:98%
So, what interested me in Mathematica at the time was the ability to do formal calculations

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.000 position:67%
and interacting with numerical calculation.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:36.000 position:97%
I teach in a school of architecture, School of Architecture Paris-Malaquais and... Paris Tech, which is an engineering school.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:44.000 position:97%
In both schools, I teach... the design of structures and the use of materials in structures.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.000 position:77%
Currently I am working with 10 doctoral students.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000 position:97%
In the laboratory, I have another architectural structure that is the School of Paris-Malaquais,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.000 position:91%
and the doctoral students, they all work with Mathematica,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:03.000 position:97%
because it actually allows us to have this important interaction in today's architecture

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000 position:66%
between the image, logic, and mathematics.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.000 position:97%
That's why I said there is a change in the way I used Mathematica.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.000 position:97%
At the beginning it was mostly for formal calculations and its impact on numerical calculations.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.000 position:98%
Today we do more numerical calculations than formal calculations.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:26.000 position:98%
Mathematica allows the interaction between geometry and the opportunity to interact with architects

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:32.000 position:97%
and interface to other programs for exporting to other useful formats.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.000 position:59%
First, there is the scientific aspect.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:46.000 position:95%
Mathematica allows me, and the doctoral students I work with,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:57.000 position:98%
to have a continuity of problem as it is understood from formal and fundamental viewpoints for programming and exporting results.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:03.000 position:98%
There is a great continuity, which means, the alternative would be to use many different tools,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.000 position:97%
or perhaps tools that are looking to be as wide but less complete.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.000 position:98%
It allows us at the same time, a magnitude of the fact that we can start from a fundamental process to applications

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:27.000 position:98%
without changing the software in a manner that we will never have to resort to other questions.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.000 position:88%
A second factor for me, as a teacher, it is in pedagogy.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:40.000 position:97%
I use Mathematica in two different ways in teaching. To show something correct, well designed, well calculated

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.000 position:75%
to students in lecture room without interaction.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:55.000 position:98%
And the other is to develop first-year and second-year students in the field,

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:01.000 position:98%
to develop tools and procedures that allow them to understand a little bit the foundation of the science,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.000 position:92%
and it is a really important thing in architecture schools.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:10.000 position:98%
The third important element has to do precisely with communication.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:24.000 position:97%
We are working on an interface that connects two worlds: architecture and engineering.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:31.000 position:97%
And these two worlds have their own uses, their own ways of saying things,

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.000 position:86%
which sometimes can create some communication problems.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:41.000 position:98%
However, the images are often used as a bridge so that everyone can talk about and understand the same thing.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:51.000 position:97%
The third thing Mathematica allows us to is after we maintained all our rigor and love for math and logic,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:57.000 position:97%
we can arrive at an exportable final result in another culture without difficulty.

